<%# The "Sign in with Google" button, for every engine page that offers Google
    (sessions/new, registrations/new, studio/profiles/_google_section).

    Locals:
      label          — REQUIRED. The button's words ("Sign in with Google").
      button_class   — optional. Default "btn btn-google btn-lg w-full gap-3".
      email_fallback — optional, default true. The modal's "Use email instead",
                       which closes it and focuses the page's email field. The
                       profile page, where the person is already signed in,
                       passes false and gets "Not now".

    TWO STATES, by Studio::GoogleSignIn.button_posts?:

      READY — the app has its OAuth client (or registered its own provider, or
      OmniAuth is in test mode). A POST form to /auth/google_oauth2, Turbo off:
      OmniAuth's middleware owns that path, and the request phase is POST-only
      and CSRF-checked.

      NOT YET — no client yet. The same button, opening a modal on a page-scoped
      host (store googleSetupModals) that says Google sign-in is still being set
      up, offers "Request Google setup" (POST /_studio/google_setup_request,
      which mails the team once per app per day) and a way back to email.

    The x-data on the wrapper is load-bearing: studio/modals/_scoped_host
    declares no Alpine scope of its own, and without one above it the modal
    registers, opens, and renders nothing (see studio/profiles/show). One button
    per page; two would mount two hosts on one store. %>
<%
  google_label = local_assigns.fetch(:label)
  google_button_class = local_assigns.fetch(:button_class, "btn btn-google btn-lg w-full gap-3")
  google_email_fallback = local_assigns.fetch(:email_fallback, true)
%>
<% if Studio::GoogleSignIn.button_posts? %>
  <%= button_to Studio::GoogleSignIn::REQUEST_PATH, method: :post, data: { turbo: false, google_sign_in: "ready" },
        class: google_button_class do %>
    <%= render "components/google_logo" %>
    <%= google_label %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <div x-data data-google-sign-in="setup">
    <button type="button" class="<%= google_button_class %>" aria-haspopup="dialog"
            @click="$store.googleSetupModals.open('google-setup')">
      <%= render "components/google_logo" %>
      <%= google_label %>
    </button>
    <%= render "studio/modals/scoped_host", store: "googleSetupModals" do %>
      <template x-if="$store.googleSetupModals.current()?.id === 'google-setup'">
        <%= render "studio/google_sign_in/setup_modal", email_fallback: google_email_fallback %>
      </template>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
